  "name": null,
  "problem": "The velocity of a car that starts moving, in meters per second, is given by the function $v(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $v(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)$ | $0$ | $10$ | $25$ | $45$ | $70$ |\n\nApproximate the acceleration ${v}^{′}(t)$ when $t=20$ using a backward difference approximation.",
